family: F3
grade: judge

--- prompt ---
The "Software listing" plugin (tt_content uid 6) was configured to show 9 items, but
the configured limit no longer reaches the plugin — reading the record's settings
returns nothing for it.

Diagnose why. Name the exact cause. Do not fix it.

--- setup ---
# The stored FlexForm XML still says settings.limit, but the data structure now calls
# the field settings.maxItems, so the stored value no longer maps to any field.
sed -i.bak 's|<settings.limit>|<settings.maxItems>|; s|</settings.limit>|</settings.maxItems>|' \
    packages/bench_fixture/Configuration/FlexForms/BenchPlugin.xml
rm -f packages/bench_fixture/Configuration/FlexForms/BenchPlugin.xml.bak
ddev exec vendor/bin/typo3 cache:flush >/dev/null 2>&1

--- oracle ---
echo "Root cause: the FlexForm data structure renamed the field settings.limit to settings.maxItems."
echo "File: packages/bench_fixture/Configuration/FlexForms/BenchPlugin.xml"
echo "The stored XML on tt_content uid 6 still carries settings.limit=9, which no longer matches any field in the DS, so it is dropped when the FlexForm is read."

--- check ---
exit 2
